# One per "has held for T" comparison in this piston. They record WHEN the
# condition became true so the piston can ask how long it has held — see
# _was_held in the runtime above for why last_changed cannot answer that.
#
# These wake on every change of the value they watch, which is unavoidable:
# knowing a predicate held CONTINUOUSLY means seeing each change. They are
# plain function calls rather than automation runs, so the cost is small, and
